{"id": "3811f67c-9e57-4f00-8da1-973a49cff7c6", "title": {"en": "Ice and Fire", "es": "Hielo y Fuego", "pt": "Gelo e Fogo"}, "card": {"foregroundColor": {"blue": 1, "green": 1, "opacity": 1, "red": 1}, "image": "", "imageStyle": "textFirst", "localizedTitle": {"en": "### Ice and Fire", "es": "### Hielo y Fuego", "pt": "### Gelo e Fogo"}}, "pages": [{"id": "d7934594-e1c9-497d-97dd-5e47a160b6a0", "blocks": [{"id": "89d01faf-666e-4e55-b520-7fd34c462264", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Geologic Background: Why Iceland\u2019s Volcanoes are so Diverse", "es": "## Contexto Geol\u00f3gico: Por Qu\u00e9 los Volcanes de Islandia Son Tan Diversos", "pt": "## Contexto Geol\u00f3gico: Por Que os Vulc\u00f5es da Isl\u00e2ndia S\u00e3o T\u00e3o Diversos"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "b81144ef-4da2-4b1b-84d4-72d1c1b480f5", "height": "huge", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "7e063e8f-c13c-4d25-ab38-6949aa81bb11", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Iceland is one of the most volcanically active places on Earth because \nof its special location. It sits right on the **Mid-Atlantic Ridge**, which \nis where two of the Earth's giant **tectonic plates** are slowly pulling away \nfrom each other. At the same time, Iceland is located over a **\"hotspot\"**, \nan unusually hot area in the Earth's crust where rocks have risen from \ndeep underground to melt, forming **magma**.\n\nThis unique combination creates many different kinds of volcanic activity. \nSome eruptions are explosive, shooting huge clouds of ash high into the sky. \nOther eruptions are calmer, with lava flowing steadily out of long cracks in \nthe ground (called **fissures**) like a river of fire. Because these eruption styles \nare so different, they create their own unique sounds and vibrations in the \nground. \n\nBy listening to these signals, scientists can understand what type of \neruption is happening. Most importantly, they can hear the warning signs of an \neruption *before* it happens, which helps them warn people and reduce the volcano's \nharmful impact.\n", "es": "Islandia es uno de los lugares con mayor actividad volc\u00e1nica de la Tierra debido \na su ubicaci\u00f3n especial. Se encuentra justo sobre la **Dorsal Mesoatl\u00e1ntica**, que es \ndonde dos de las gigantes **placas tect\u00f3nicas** de la Tierra se est\u00e1n separando lentamente. \nAl mismo tiempo, Islandia est\u00e1 situada sobre un **\u201cpunto caliente\u201d**, una zona inusualmente \ncaliente en la corteza terrestre donde las rocas han ascendido desde gran profundidad \npara fundirse y formar **magma**.\n\nEsta combinaci\u00f3n \u00fanica genera muchos tipos diferentes de actividad volc\u00e1nica. \nAlgunas erupciones son explosivas y lanzan enormes nubes de ceniza a gran altura \nen el cielo. Otras erupciones son m\u00e1s tranquilas, con lava que fluye de manera \nconstante a trav\u00e9s de largas grietas en el suelo (llamadas **fisuras**), como un \nr\u00edo de fuego. Debido a que estos estilos de erupci\u00f3n son tan distintos, \nproducen sonidos y vibraciones \u00fanicas en el terreno.\n\nAl escuchar estas se\u00f1ales, los cient\u00edficos pueden comprender qu\u00e9 tipo de \nerupci\u00f3n est\u00e1 ocurriendo. Lo m\u00e1s importante es que pueden detectar las se\u00f1ales \nde advertencia de una erupci\u00f3n *antes* de que suceda, lo que les ayuda a alertar \na las personas y a reducir el impacto da\u00f1ino del volc\u00e1n.\n", "pt": "A Isl\u00e2ndia \u00e9 um dos lugares mais vulcanicamente ativos da Terra por causa de \nsua localiza\u00e7\u00e3o especial. Ela est\u00e1 situada exatamente sobre a **Dorsal Mesoatl\u00e2ntica**, \nque \u00e9 onde duas das gigantes **placas tect\u00f4nicas** da Terra est\u00e3o lentamente se \nafastando uma da outra. Ao mesmo tempo, a Isl\u00e2ndia est\u00e1 localizada sobre um **\u201chotspot\u201d**, \numa \u00e1rea excepcionalmente quente na crosta terrestre onde rochas ascenderam de \ngrandes profundidades, derreteram e formaram **magma**.\n\nEssa combina\u00e7\u00e3o \u00fanica cria muitos tipos diferentes de atividade vulc\u00e2nica. \nAlgumas erup\u00e7\u00f5es s\u00e3o explosivas, lan\u00e7ando enormes nuvens de cinzas bem \nalto no c\u00e9u. Outras erup\u00e7\u00f5es s\u00e3o mais calmas, com a lava fluindo de forma \nconstante a partir de longas rachaduras no solo (chamadas **fissuras**), \ncomo um rio de fogo. Como esses estilos de erup\u00e7\u00e3o s\u00e3o t\u00e3o diferentes, \neles produzem sons e vibra\u00e7\u00f5es \u00fanicos no solo.\n\nAo ouvir esses sinais, os cientistas conseguem entender que tipo de erup\u00e7\u00e3o \nest\u00e1 acontecendo. Mais importante ainda, eles podem identificar os sinais de \nalerta de uma erup\u00e7\u00e3o antes que ela aconte\u00e7a, o que ajuda a avisar as pessoas \ne a reduzir o impacto prejudicial do vulc\u00e3o.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "d2095fb7-7196-4e85-8e6c-76e8a081f73a", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "Image: ***Litli-Hr\u00fatur - Volcanic Eruption in Iceland July 2023*** by ***Anthony Quintano.*** Licensed under CC BY 2.0", "es": "Imagen: ***Litli-Hr\u00fatur - Volcanic Eruption in Iceland July 2023*** by ***Anthony Quintano.*** Licensed under CC BY 2.0", "pt": "Imagem: ***Litli-Hr\u00fatur - Volcanic Eruption in Iceland July 2023*** by ***Anthony Quintano.*** Licensed under CC BY 2.0"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "d84df6a3-5c15-4d61-8434-e4dd1e776c79", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "P1. Comparing Iceland\u2019s Eruptions"}, {"id": "9ef9a0d5-3dce-428f-9209-163f0c1e022b", "blocks": [{"id": "82e2c736-1a30-4d1a-9545-6587a0edf9cc", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Comparing Iceland\u2019s Eruptions", "es": "## Comparando las Erupciones en Islandia", "pt": "## Comparando as Erup\u00e7\u00f5es na Isl\u00e2ndia"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "c1cb6dd5-59e5-4cd7-a93e-74391a96a3dd", "height": "huge", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "ffc8ce03-5e8c-4d37-ac82-96706721b870", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Let's compare the sounds of two very different Icelandic eruptions.\n\nFirst, listen to the 2010 eruption of the Eyjafjallaj\u00f6kull volcano. \nThis was a highly explosive event from a tall, cone-shaped volcano \ncovered by a **glacier**. The magma inside was very thick and sticky. \n\nWhen this super-hot, sticky magma mixed with the ice, it caused a \nmassive steam explosion that blasted out a giant cloud of ash. \nThis ash cloud famously shut down air travel across Europe for weeks.\n", "es": "Comparemos los sonidos de dos erupciones islandesas muy diferentes.\n\nPrimero, escuchemos la erupci\u00f3n de 2010 del volc\u00e1n Eyjafjallaj\u00f6kull. \nFue un evento altamente explosivo proveniente de un volc\u00e1n alto, \ncon forma de cono, cubierto por un **glaciar**. El magma en su interior \nera muy espeso y pegajoso.\n\nCuando este magma extremadamente caliente y viscoso se mezcl\u00f3 con el hielo, \nprovoc\u00f3 una enorme explosi\u00f3n de vapor que lanz\u00f3 una gigantesca nube de ceniza. \nEsta nube de ceniza, de forma famosa, paraliz\u00f3 el tr\u00e1fico a\u00e9reo en toda \nEuropa durante semanas.\n", "pt": "Vamos comparar os sons de duas erup\u00e7\u00f5es islandesas muito diferentes.\n\nPrimeiro, vamos ouvir a erup\u00e7\u00e3o de 2010 do vulc\u00e3o Eyjafjallaj\u00f6kull. \nEsse foi um evento altamente explosivo de um vulc\u00e3o alto, em forma de cone, \ncoberto por uma **geleira**. O magma em seu interior era muito espesso e pegajoso.\n\nQuando esse magma superquente e viscoso se misturou com o gelo, ocorreu \numa enorme explos\u00e3o de vapor que lan\u00e7ou uma gigantesca nuvem de cinzas. \nEssa nuvem de cinzas ficou famosa por interromper o tr\u00e1fego a\u00e9reo em \ntoda a Europa por semanas.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "1a3623a6-7498-4db0-919c-aa3402677fb9", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Pyroclastic Eruption:", "es": "Erupci\u00f3n Pirocl\u00e1stica:", "pt": "Erup\u00e7\u00e3o Pirocl\u00e1stica:"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "b1db12d6-7914-49f9-bbfa-42560b17b2c7", "octavesHigher": 1024, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 7200, "startDate": "2010-04-15T16:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "4DEE77F4-3865-4DA1-83AF-E522FA2A91A5", "name": "Iceland", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "II", "station": "BORG"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "a4cfbc27-7be3-40e7-b277-f340e502e906", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Next, listen to the eruption that began on December 18, 2023, on the Reykjanes Peninsula. \nThis was a **fissure eruption**, where lava flowed from a long crack in the ground. \nThe lava was thin and runny, so it produced spectacular rivers of lava but very little ash.\n", "es": "A continuaci\u00f3n, escuchemos la erupci\u00f3n que comenz\u00f3 el 18 de diciembre de 2023 en la pen\u00ednsula \nde Reykjanes. Se trat\u00f3 de una **erupci\u00f3n fisural**, en la que la lava fluy\u00f3 desde una larga grieta \nen el suelo. La lava era delgada y fluida, por lo que produjo espectaculares r\u00edos de lava, \npero muy poca ceniza.\n", "pt": "Em seguida, vamos ouvir a erup\u00e7\u00e3o que come\u00e7ou em 18 de dezembro de 2023, na Pen\u00ednsula \nde Reykjanes. Foi uma **erup\u00e7\u00e3o fissural**, na qual a lava fluiu a partir de uma longa \nfenda no solo. A lava era fina e muito fluida, o que produziu rios espetaculares de lava, \nmas pouqu\u00edssima cinza.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "3997c65b-9a05-495d-a61c-1aee9ddb67df", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Fissure Eruption:", "es": "Erupci\u00f3n Fisural:", "pt": "Erup\u00e7\u00e3o Fissural:"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "a6d6990b-49f4-46f5-b454-44ebaa9b5a29", "octavesHigher": 1024, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 7200, "startDate": "2023-12-18T22:30:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "808CDF29-A34C-4D70-9DFD-0A084B00B24A", "name": "Iceland", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "II", "station": "BORG"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "45d633ab-065b-470d-b0bc-63fd5a8d05f7", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}, {"id": "05948b26-a6de-4222-9a96-3d760d045084", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "Image: ***Litli-Hr\u00fatur - Volcanic Eruption in Iceland July 2023*** by ***Anthony Quintano.*** Licensed under CC BY 2.0", "es": "Imagen: ***Litli-Hr\u00fatur - Volcanic Eruption in Iceland July 2023*** by ***Anthony Quintano.*** Licensed under CC BY 2.0", "pt": "Imagem: ***Litli-Hr\u00fatur - Volcanic Eruption in Iceland July 2023*** by ***Anthony Quintano.*** Licensed under CC BY 2.0"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}], "title": "P2. Listening for Warning Signs"}, {"id": "1f7f8790-fa9d-4a6d-902d-a7836f37f043", "blocks": [{"id": "67fd7029-e6b0-406a-98e6-5137c6d85cb9", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Listening for Warning Signs", "es": "## Escuchando las Se\u00f1ales de Advertencia", "pt": "## Ouvindo os Sinais de Alerta"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "1b9fcb52-9284-4c3d-a3d6-5d8799504b9c", "height": "regular", "image": "", "type": "image"}, {"id": "67d96eb3-bff1-4275-a321-380cdb4c18a0", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "The December 2023 eruption did not happen without warning. For weeks beforehand, \nscientists tracked thousands of small earthquakes as a **dike of magma** - a vertical \nsheet of molten rock - forced its way toward the surface. This intense **seismic activity**, \nknown as an **earthquake swarm**, was a clear sign of an impending eruption. \n\nFirst, listen to a seismically \u201cquiet\u201d day in the region before the major unrest began.\n", "es": "La erupci\u00f3n de diciembre de 2023 no ocurri\u00f3 sin advertencia. Durante semanas previas, \nlos cient\u00edficos registraron miles de peque\u00f1os terremotos mientras un **dique de magma**\n\u2014 una l\u00e1mina vertical de roca fundida \u2014 se abr\u00eda paso hacia la superficie. \nEsta intensa **actividad s\u00edsmica**, conocida como un **enjambre de terremotos**, fue una \nse\u00f1al clara de una erupci\u00f3n inminente.\n\nPrimero, escuchemos un d\u00eda s\u00edsmicamente \u201ctranquilo\u201d en la regi\u00f3n, \nantes de que comenzara la principal fase de agitaci\u00f3n.\n", "pt": "A erup\u00e7\u00e3o de dezembro de 2023 n\u00e3o aconteceu sem aviso pr\u00e9vio. Durante semanas antes,\nos cientistas acompanharam milhares de pequenos terremotos \u00e0 medida que um **dique de \nmagma** \u2014 uma l\u00e2mina vertical de rocha derretida \u2014 for\u00e7ava seu caminho em dire\u00e7\u00e3o \u00e0 \nsuperf\u00edcie. Essa intensa **atividade s\u00edsmica**, conhecida como um **enxame de terremotos**, \nfoi um sinal claro de uma erup\u00e7\u00e3o iminente.\n\nPrimeiro, vamos ouvir um dia sismicamente \u201ccalmo\u201d na regi\u00e3o, \nantes do in\u00edcio da principal fase de agita\u00e7\u00e3o.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "32228343-e93e-47c9-9b8c-53f240186f8d", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Before Eruption (Baseline)", "es": "Antes de la Erupci\u00f3n (L\u00ednea Base)", "pt": "Antes da Erup\u00e7\u00e3o (Linha de Base)"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "f6f2c2b1-fbb3-49c6-8133-b619bbd12866", "octavesHigher": 1024, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 7200, "startDate": "2023-09-18T22:30:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "808CDF29-A567-4D70-9DFD-0A084B00B24A", "name": "Iceland", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "II", "station": "BORG"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "f151f689-9cf6-42b7-bbc6-86fc5f44b2a9", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Now, listen to the intense earthquake swarm from November 10, 2023. \nThis activity is what led to the evacuation of the nearby town of Grindav\u00edk. \nThe sound is like a hailstorm, where each \"pellet\" you hear is a small \nearthquake. These quakes were caused by rock cracking apart deep underground as \nmagma, or melted rock, pushed its way toward the surface.\n", "es": "Ahora, escuchemos el intenso enjambre de terremotos del 10 de noviembre de 2023. \nEsta actividad fue la que llev\u00f3 a la evacuaci\u00f3n de la ciudad cercana de Grindav\u00edk. \nEl sonido es similar al de una tormenta de granizo, donde cada \u201cgranizo\u201d \nque se escucha es un peque\u00f1o terremoto. Estos sismos fueron causados por \nla fractura de las rocas en las profundidades del subsuelo, a medida que el \nmagma, o roca fundida, avanzaba hacia la superficie.\n", "pt": "Agora, vamos ouvir o intenso enxame de terremotos de 10 de novembro de 2023. \nEssa atividade foi o que levou \u00e0 evacua\u00e7\u00e3o da cidade pr\u00f3xima de Grindav\u00edk. \nO som se assemelha ao de uma tempestade de granizo, em que cada \u201cpedra\u201d que \nse ouve \u00e9 um pequeno terremoto. Esses abalos foram causados pela fratura das \nrochas em profundidade, \u00e0 medida que o magma, ou rocha derretida, for\u00e7ava \nseu caminho em dire\u00e7\u00e3o \u00e0 superf\u00edcie.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "b28b5b5e-6691-43ab-9396-6cb31131a1c3", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "Leading Up to Eruption", "es": "En los Momentos Previos a la Erupci\u00f3n", "pt": "Nos Momentos que Antecedem a Erup\u00e7\u00e3o"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "7d1f55f3-f0b4-4334-b062-57e2c7bc01e3", "octavesHigher": 1024, "type": "localWave", "volumeModifier": "fixed", "waveData": {"duration": 7200, "startDate": "2023-11-10T16:00:00Z", "station": {"group": "user", "id": "808CDF29-A567-4D70-922D-0A084B00B24A", "name": "Iceland", "periods": [{"channel": "BHZ", "location": "00", "network": "II", "station": "BORG"}], "preferredTimeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}, "timeLatency": 0}, "timeZone": {"identifier": "GMT", "style": "byGMTValue"}}}, {"id": "a5ddd9f6-82f7-477c-9e72-5e091a531cad", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question** Compare the sounds from the \"quiet\" day and the day of \nthe **earthquake swarm**. How can listening to this major change in the \nEarth's vibrations help scientists and community leaders decide what \nto do to protect people?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** Compara los sonidos del d\u00eda \u201ctranquilo\u201d y del d\u00eda del \n**enjambre de terremotos**. \u00bfC\u00f3mo puede escuchar este gran cambio en las \nvibraciones de la Tierra ayudar a los cient\u00edficos y a los l\u00edderes \ncomunitarios a decidir qu\u00e9 hacer para proteger a las personas?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Compare os sons do dia \u201ccalmo\u201d e do dia do **enxame de \nterremotos**. Como escutar essa mudan\u00e7a significativa nas vibra\u00e7\u00f5es da Terra \npode ajudar cientistas e l\u00edderes comunit\u00e1rios a decidir o que fazer \npara proteger as pessoas?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "99263868-68df-4f14-ac34-d984a15bb605", "action": "next", "localizedText": {"en": "Next", "es": "Siguiente", "pt": "Pr\u00f3ximo"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}, {"id": "ce02a214-f80f-4592-b593-e5ae6ee7eb51", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "Image: ***Volcanic Eruption*** by ***Sigfried Makedanz.*** Licensed under CC BY-NC 2.0", "es": "Imagen: ***Volcanic Eruption*** by ***Sigfried Makedanz.*** Licensed under CC BY-NC 2.0", "pt": "Imagem: ***Volcanic Eruption*** by ***Sigfried Makedanz.*** Licensed under CC BY-NC 2.0"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}], "title": "P3. Living Among Volcanoes"}, {"id": "472344e3-387f-4372-8cd6-56f2d4b13551", "blocks": [{"id": "9a387e3d-189e-4ace-8be0-3d398b0e8462", "backgroundTransparent": true, "localizedText": {"en": "## Living Among Volcanoes", "es": "## Viviendo Entre Volcanes", "pt": "## Vivendo Entre Vulc\u00f5es"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": true}, {"id": "6be46ed8-1612-4ac6-be72-3b76c72fd230", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "The warnings from the earthquake swarms gave Icelandic officials the \nimportant time they needed to act. In November 2023, they evacuated \nthe entire town of Grindav\u00edk, asking all 4,000 residents to leave their \nhomes for safety.\n\nBecause an eruption seemed certain to happen, engineers raced to build \nhuge walls made of earth and rock. These walls, called berms were designed \nto protect both the town and a nearby power plant from the expected lava flows.\n\nWhen the volcano finally erupted, these protective efforts were very successful. \nAlthough some lava reached the edge of town and destroyed three homes, the \nbarriers turned the main lava flow away. This saved the rest of the town and \nits important services, like power and water, from being destroyed. The story \nof Grindav\u00edk is a powerful example of how listening to earthquakes, forecasting \neruptions, and smart engineering can help people live more safely alongside volcanoes.\n", "es": "Las advertencias provenientes de los enjambres de terremotos dieron a las \nautoridades islandesas el tiempo crucial que necesitaban para actuar. \nEn noviembre de 2023, evacuaron por completo la ciudad de Grindav\u00edk, \npidiendo a los 4.000 habitantes que abandonaran sus hogares por seguridad.\n\nComo parec\u00eda seguro que ocurrir\u00eda una erupci\u00f3n, los ingenieros se apresuraron \na construir enormes muros de tierra y roca. Estos muros, llamados bermas, fueron \ndise\u00f1ados para proteger tanto a la ciudad como a una central el\u00e9ctrica cercana \nde los flujos de lava esperados.\n\nCuando el volc\u00e1n finalmente entr\u00f3 en erupci\u00f3n, estas medidas de protecci\u00f3n resultaron \nmuy exitosas. Aunque parte de la lava alcanz\u00f3 el borde de la ciudad y destruy\u00f3 tres \nviviendas, las barreras desviaron el flujo principal de lava. Esto salv\u00f3 al resto \nde la ciudad y a sus servicios esenciales, como la electricidad y el agua, de ser \ndestruidos. La historia de Grindav\u00edk es un poderoso ejemplo de c\u00f3mo escuchar a los \nterremotos, pronosticar erupciones y aplicar una ingenier\u00eda inteligente puede ayudar \na las personas a vivir de forma m\u00e1s segura junto a los volcanes.\n", "pt": "Os alertas gerados pelos enxames de terremotos deram \u00e0s autoridades islandesas o \ntempo essencial de que precisavam para agir. Em novembro de 2023, elas evacuaram \ntoda a cidade de Grindav\u00edk, pedindo que os 4.000 moradores deixassem suas casas \npor seguran\u00e7a.\n\nComo parecia certo que uma erup\u00e7\u00e3o iria acontecer, engenheiros correram para \nconstruir enormes barreiras de terra e rocha. Essas estruturas, chamadas de bermas, \nforam projetadas para proteger tanto a cidade quanto uma usina de energia pr\u00f3xima \ndos fluxos de lava esperados.\n\nQuando o vulc\u00e3o finalmente entrou em erup\u00e7\u00e3o, essas medidas de prote\u00e7\u00e3o foram \nmuito bem-sucedidas. Embora parte da lava tenha alcan\u00e7ado a borda da cidade e \ndestru\u00eddo tr\u00eas casas, as barreiras desviaram o principal fluxo de lava. \nIsso salvou o restante da cidade e seus servi\u00e7os essenciais, como energia el\u00e9trica \ne abastecimento de \u00e1gua, de serem destru\u00eddos. A hist\u00f3ria de Grindav\u00edk \u00e9 um exemplo \npoderoso de como ouvir os terremotos, prever erup\u00e7\u00f5es e usar engenharia inteligente \npode ajudar as pessoas a viver com mais seguran\u00e7a ao lado dos vulc\u00f5es.\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "ebe42107-a86f-4fed-af07-90cefcbc673e", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 1.** Based on the seismic warnings you heard, why was it so important for \nauthorities to act quickly to evacuate Grindav\u00edk and build protective barriers? \n", "es": "**Pregunta 1.** Con base en las advertencias s\u00edsmicas que escuchaste, \n\u00bfpor qu\u00e9 fue tan importante que las autoridades actuaran con rapidez para \nevacuar Grindav\u00edk y construir barreras de protecci\u00f3n?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 1.** Com base nos alertas s\u00edsmicos que voc\u00ea ouviu, por que foi t\u00e3o \nimportante que as autoridades agissem rapidamente para evacuar Grindav\u00edk \ne construir barreiras de prote\u00e7\u00e3o?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "fab084d3-d067-4e91-b4fa-86e766b92a57", "backgroundTransparent": false, "localizedText": {"en": "**Question 2.** What challenges might communities face when asked to evacuate \ntheir homes based on a forecast, before an eruption has even begun?\n", "es": "**Pregunta 2.** \u00bfQu\u00e9 desaf\u00edos podr\u00edan enfrentar las comunidades cuando se les \npide evacuar sus hogares bas\u00e1ndose en un pron\u00f3stico, incluso antes de que \nhaya comenzado una erupci\u00f3n?\n", "pt": "**Pergunta 2.** Quais desafios as comunidades podem enfrentar quando s\u00e3o \nsolicitadas a evacuar suas casas com base em uma previs\u00e3o, antes mesmo \nde uma erup\u00e7\u00e3o come\u00e7ar?\n"}, "type": "markdown", "underlined": false}, {"id": "86e7ec9c-b0d6-4915-8fea-468ba2b9ea15", "action": "close", "localizedText": {"en": "Close", "es": "Cerrar", "pt": "Fechar"}, "paramValue": "", "type": "button"}], "title": "P4. More Wastewater from oil and gas drilling"}]}